ares chip code in the snes9x core and in recompiled SNES carts  (ISC)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
  The firmware-running SNES coprocessors (the ST010/ST011 NEC uPD96050 and the
  ST018 ARM) are compiled from ares (https://github.com/ares-emulator/ares, at
  the commit pinned in romdevtools/scripts/versions.json, cores.ares): its
  processor cores ares/component/processor/upd96050 and arm7tdmi, the Super
  Famicom driver files ares/sfc/coprocessor/necdsp/memory.cpp and
  armdsp/memory.cpp and io.cpp, and the nall headers they use, with romdev's
  glue (romdevtools/scripts/recompile-gen/ares-chips/glue/, MIT) restating the
  rest of those drivers and ares's thread clock. That code is compiled into:
    - recompiled SNES carts built with options.firmware (ST011 / ST018): the
      units in romdevtools/src/analysis/recompile/wat/snes/ares-chips.json;
    - romdev's snes9x core (romdev-platform-snes, snes9x-ares-chips.patch),
      used when st011.rom / st018.rom is in the system directory.
  ares is under the ISC license, a permissive license whose only condition is
  keeping its notice, so it can sit with snes9x's non-commercial license and
  with romdev's MIT code. A recompiled cart or a snes9x core build that
  contains it carries this notice:

    ares

