    Permission to use, copy, modify, and/or distribute this software for any
    purpose with or without fee is hereby granted, provided that the above
    copyright notice and this permission notice appear in all copies.

    THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND THE AUTHOR DISCLAIMS ALL WARRANTIES
    WITH REGARD TO THIS SOFTWARE INCLUDING ALL IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF
    MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHOR BE LIABLE FOR
    ANY SPECIAL, DIRECT, INDIRECT, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES OR ANY DAMAGES
    WHATSOEVER RESULTING FROM LOSS OF USE, DATA OR PROFITS, WHETHER IN AN
    ACTION OF CONTRACT, NEGLIGENCE OR OTHER TORTIOUS ACTION, ARISING OUT OF
    OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE USE OR PERFORMANCE OF THIS SOFTWARE.

  A recompiled SNES cart's machine follows snes9x and carries snes9x's own
  chip units, so those parts of a cart stay under snes9x's non-commercial
  license, as before; the ares code adds no condition of its own. No bsnes
  (GPL-3.0) code is compiled into snes9x or into a cart: bsnes ships only as
  its own core, romdev-core-bsnes. No coprocessor firmware ships with romdev.

C64 ROMs - free replacements, not Commodore's
----------------------------------------------
  Upstream vice-libretro compiles Commodore's KERNAL, BASIC and CHARGEN ROMs
  into the core (USE_EMBEDDED). Those images are "Copyright C by Commodore
  Business Machines" per VICE's own README; the GPL covers VICE's code, not
  them. romdev builds VICE with that define disabled and redistributes none of
  them.

  In their place romdev-core-vice bundles MEGA65 Open ROMs (GPL-3.0 /
  LGPL-3.0), a clean-room KERNAL/BASIC/CHARGEN, so the C64 works out of the
  box. Licences ship alongside the images in that package's roms/ directory.
  Set ROMDEV_C64_ROM_DIR to use original ROMs you own instead.

